-- Reading: short texts and their main topic.

Every summer, Greenhill Library runs a reading club for children aged seven to twelve. Children borrow books, write a few words about each one in a small notebook and collect a sticker for every book they finish. The club is free. It starts on the first Monday of July and ends in the last week of August. Children who read six books receive a certificate at a party in the library garden. Parents can sign their children up at the front desk.', 'VALID');
